      "ground": "102",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1"],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The Examiner finds Hutchins (U.S. Pat. No. 5,268,112) discloses mixing aqueous gel-forming ingredients including silicates and polymeric components with delayed-acting substances (esters, anhydrides) or gas precursors and placing the resulting composition into subterranean formations to occupy pores and reduce permeability. Hutchins explicitly teaches such compositions, the use of esters/anhydrides as delay agents, pumping into formations, and occupying pores to reduce permeability; these teachings anticipate the generic limitations of claims 1–7 and claim 19 as currently presented.",
