        {
          "doc_id": "IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1",
          "support_span": "Claims 1-7 and claim 19 are rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 102(b) as being anticipated by US Patent 5268112 (Hutchins).",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1",
          "support_span": "Hutchins teaches a method comprises mixing in aqueous media a gel-forming ingredient with a gas precursor such as urea and a delayed acting substance such as esters, anhydrides to form a gellable composition",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    },
    {
      "claim_ids": [11,12,13,14,15,16,17,18],
      "ground": "103",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1"],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "Even where Hutchins does not recite the particular sequence of pumping first a portion of initiator, then composition, then a second portion, ordering of process steps such as mixing/order of injection is recognized as an obvious design choice absent evidence of an unexpected result. The cited portions of Hutchins teach the relevant components (silicates, polymers, delayed-acting esters/anhydrides, CO2/gas precursors) and their use in subterranean treatments. Given that teaching, modifying the order of injection or separating the initiator into portions would have been an obvious variation to a person of ordinary skill.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1",
          "support_span": "Claims 11-18 are rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 103(a) as being unpatentable over Hutchins.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "IP70AMJ4RXEAPX1",
          "support_span": "selection of any order of performing process steps or selection of any order of mixing ingredients is prima facie obvious in the absence of new or unexpected results. In re Burhans ... In re Gibson ...",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
