      "argument_summary": "Applicant amended claim 1 to recite a 'toroidally wound magnet' and argues MIT teaches only different tape widths between pancakes (axially in the stack) and does not teach varying tape width within a single pancake (radially). Applicant contends MIT teaches away from intra-pancake width variation and therefore cannot anticipate claim 1.",
      "response": "The examiner acknowledges the applicant's amendment and argument emphasizing intra-pancake radial variation. The prior Office action relied on MIT for multi-width conductor teachings and on Young (and other cited art) to supply toroidal magnet structure and plate/shell support teachings. On the present record, the examiner finds that the cited MIT disclosure (as relied upon in O1) and the applied secondary toroidal teachings provide a basis for the asserted rejections against the amended claim set. However, if applicant wishes to distinguish the claim over MIT on the precise point that MIT only varies width between pancakes and not within a single turn/radially within a pancake, applicant should (a) identify specific, supportable record passages or evidence showing MIT lacks any disclosure or suggestion of intra-pancake/radial tape-width variation and (b) propose claim language that more precisely captures the intended radial-within-a-turn limitation (for example, explicit recitation of 'varying tape width along an individual turn from an inner radial position to an outer radial position within a single pancake coil') so the record clearly reflects the distinguishing feature. Absent a clear record showing MIT cannot be read to disclose or suggest the claimed toroidal implementations, the prior rejection is maintained. ",
