      "rationale": "Claim 7 (thickness of haptic plate greater than any portion of the connector) was rejected as obvious over Blake in view of Richardson in the prior Office action. The applicant's amendment to claim 1 adds a filament limitation but does not alter the plate-vs-connector thickness relationship recited in claim 7. The record evidence (prior Office action) asserts Richardson teaches connectors (arms) thinner than haptic plate portions; combining that teaching with Blake's teachings regarding varying plate thickness would have made the claimed plate/connector thickness relationship obvious. Therefore the 103 rejection for claim 7 is maintained.",
