      "argument_summary": "Applicant did not specifically argue claim 7 in the remarks but asserted dependent claims are allowable because dependent claims depend from allowable independent claim 1.",
      "response": "Claim 7 is dependent on claim 1 but recites an additional structural relationship (plate thickness greater than connector). The presence of filaments in amended claim 1 does not avoid the combination of Blake and Richardson relied upon in the prior Office action for claim 7. The Examiner's position is that Richardson teaches thinner connector/arm constructions relative to a plate, and Blake teaches varying plate thickness; combining these teachings would have made the thickness relationship recited in claim 7 obvious to a person of ordinary skill. Therefore the 103 rejection for claim 7 is maintained. If Applicant believes claim 7 is patentable in view of the cited references, Applicant should either (a) present argument explaining why the combination of Blake and Richardson would not render claim 7 obvious (specifically identify portions of the references and explain why those teachings cannot be combined), or (b) further amend claim 7 to add features not shown or suggested in the combination of Blake and Richardson.",
