      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The Office action (O1) identified Eerolainen as anticipating these claims. The examiner's prior action characterizes Eerolainen as disclosing IRAT measurement reporting and prioritizing measurement scheduling. Applicant amended independent claims 1, 6, 11 and 16 to add express 'by the user equipment (UE)' language for the prioritizing limitation and argues Eerolainen discloses network-side prioritization rather than UE-side prioritization. The record shows the examiner's position that Eerolainen teaches prioritizing IRAT measurement scheduling; however the O1 does not include the full Eerolainen text in this file wrapper. In view of (a) the examiner's prior identification of Eerolainen as disclosing the prioritized measurement scheduling functionality and (b) the examiner's understanding that Eerolainen teaches the feature broadly enough to anticipate the independent claims as amended, the 35 U.S.C. 102(a)(1) rejections are maintained for the cited claims. If applicant wishes to overcome the rejection on the ground that Eerolainen only teaches network-side prioritization and not UE-performed prioritization, applicant should (1) point to explicit passages in Eerolainen showing the limitation is absent or (2) amend the claims to recite the structural/algorithmic means by which the UE itself performs prioritization.",
