      ],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The Office action (O1) relies on Eerolainen plus Mark to supply teaching of changing measurement frequency (increasing or decreasing) to arrive at the dependent claim limitations. The examiner found that Mark teaches varying neighbor-cell measurement frequency and Eerolainen teaches prioritized measurement scheduling; combining the teachings renders the recited frequency modifications obvious. Applicant's remarks did not present persuasive evidence or reasoning that the cited combination fails to teach the claimed features. Therefore the 35 U.S.C. 103 rejections are maintained. Applicant may rebut by (a) submitting argument or evidence that Mark does not disclose the specific frequency changes as applied to the prioritized neighbor list, or (b) amending the claims to include more specific, distinguishing steps, structure, or results.",
