      "response": "The Office cited combinations of references (Hubauer + Eiter; Hubauer + Eiter + Vasseur) for the multi-element claim limitations (mathematical RAP formulation; hypergraph solution; label-based Pareto path pruning). The record identifies particular portions of Eiter and Vasseur the Office relied upon. Applicant's argument that the references are inapposite because they do not use the same vocabulary is not sufficient by itself to overcome a references-based rejection: the proper test is whether the claimed subject matter would have been taught or rendered obvious to a skilled artisan by the combined teachings. Applicant has not presented documentary evidence or claim amendments that specifically exclude the cited teachings or narrow the claims to patentable distinction. If applicant believes a reference is being mischaracterized, applicant should identify the exact passages of the cited references and explain why those passages do not supply the claimed limitation. Alternatively, applicant may amend claims to recite distinguishing structural or procedural features that are supported by the specification.",
      "support_doc_id": "IYW27NTZRXEAPX0",
