  "applicant_argument_responses": [
    {
      "claim_ids": [1,22,31],
      "argument_summary": "Applicant states replacement drawings were filed and that Figure 3 in the provisional application (61/637,413) shows that IDA-Zn functionalization has improved antimicrobial effect (claiming the apparent contrary appearance in the originally filed Figure 3 is due to an image conversion/shading issue). Applicant requests withdrawal of the §112 and §101 rejections.",
      "response": "The Examiner acknowledges receipt of the replacement drawings filed 8/18/2014 (HZ2PPVOZPXXIFW2) and that replacement Figure 3 has been submitted. However, withdrawal of the rejections is not appropriate at this time. The record relied upon in the June 5, 2014 Office action (HVZIDU1VPXXIFW4) explicitly analyzes the Figure 3 image that was in the prosecution record at the time and concludes that the Example 3 data, as that Figure appears in the record, do not demonstrate the claimed antimicrobial efficacy for the examined species. To overcome the written-description/enablement and utility rejections, applicant must provide record evidence that demonstrates possession and operability of the recited species. This may be done by any of the following, each of which should be submitted promptly: (1) a clear, unambiguous replacement Figure 3 entered into the record that accurately and legibly presents the experimental results (the replacement drawings you submitted will be entered and considered), and a signed statement or declaration under 37 C.F.R. § 1.132 from an appropriate witness (e.g., an author of the experiment) identifying and explaining the data and asserting that the corrected Figure 3 is an accurate representation of the experimental results; and/or (2) a copy of the cited provisional application Figure 3 and a certified copy of the provisional specification and Figures if the applicant relies on the provisional to show possession and enablement; and/or (3) additional experimental data (with an explanation of methods, quantities, controls, and results) submitted in the specification or as a statement/declaration that demonstrates that the porcine ECM covalently bound to IDA and functionalized with Zn (and, if asserted, with lysostaphin) exhibits the claimed antimicrobial activity. Absent such evidence in the record, the Examiner will maintain the §112(a) (written description/enablement) and §101 rejections for the examined claims because the current record supports the Examiner's findings. For clarity: replacing the drawing file alone without an accompanying explanation/declaration or supporting data that addresses the Examiner's analysis will not, by itself, discharge the burden to show possession and operability.",
