    {
      "claim_ids": [16,17,19,20,31],
      "argument_summary": "Applicant argues that the specification (and provisional) teaches covalent binding of IDA to ECM, activation chemistries (NHS, epoxides), and functionalization with Zn, and that the examples (including Example 3) demonstrate methods and concentrations.",
      "response": "The specification does contain disclosure of chelators, activating agents, and metals and describes Example 3. The Examiner's 112 and 101 concerns focus on whether the record demonstrates possession and operability of the currently-elected species (porcine ECM covalently bound to IDA and functionalized with Zn) for the asserted antimicrobial purpose. If applicant provides the clarifying evidence requested above (declaration and/or certified provisional copy and/or additional experimental data that directly demonstrates antimicrobial activity for the examined species), the Examiner will reevaluate the 112 and 101 grounds in light of that evidence. At present, the Examiner cannot accept an assertion that the specification alone (as currently in the record) overcomes the specific factual objection the Examiner raised regarding Example 3 and Figure 3.",
