      "response": "For the system claim, the same reasoning applies. Benveniste teaches modules that perform RTS/CTS exchanges on channels and Fontaine supplies the teaching that the RTS and CTS may be transmitted on different physical channels and widths. The combination renders the recited system modules that send/receive on respective collections of fundamental channels obvious, including the numerical relationship when a skilled artisan implements Fontaine’s described channel-width arrangement using standard minimum-bandwidth channels. Therefore the rejection under 35 U.S.C. 103 is maintained for the reasons stated in the prior Office action and recited above.",
