      "rationale": "Claim 6 recites a release mechanism comprising a pair of members pivotally mounted to the bottom portion with portions received in a feature of the upper rail extension. The examiner previously rejected the corresponding claim limitations as obvious in view of the combination of Brown (teaching a pivotal member received in a feature) with any of Swan, Troy, Daniel or E'Nama (disclosing the basic modular rail structure). Applicant has not amended claim 6 to distinguish over Brown or explained why Brown's teaching would not have been combined with the other references; thus the pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 103(a) rejection over Brown in view of the other references is maintained for claim 6.",
