      ],
      "argument_summary": "Applicant amended claims to add that the upper portion/upper rail extension \"has a rail portion and a pair of side members defining an opening proximate to an end of the rail portion ... located between the rail portion ... and the top rail of the upper receiver when ... secured\" and asserted these limitations are not taught by the cited references. Applicant also argued that the 112 rejections were addressed by providing antecedent basis.",
      "response": "112(b): The 35 U.S.C. 112(b) rejections previously applied to claims that lacked proper antecedent basis are withdrawn for the amended claims. Applicant’s amendments (I40JLR5YPXXIFW3) supply the antecedent and definiteness previously found lacking. 102/103 (prior art): The amendments add a structural limitation — a pair of side members defining an opening positioned between the upper rail portion of the extension/upper portion and the top rail of the upper receiver when assembled. The prior art applied in the last action (Swan, Troy, Daniel, E'Nama) was relied upon for openings proximate a distal end or proximate a sight, and for extension/attachable rails. The examiner has re-evaluated those references against the newly-added limitation and, based on the explanation below, withdraws the pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 102 rejections that asserted anticipation of claims 1, 7, 16 and 19. No new matter appears to have been added; support for the amendment is present in the specification (record). However, the previously maintained obviousness rejection over Brown in view of the other references for the pivotally-mounted member limitation (claim 6) remains because Applicant did not amend claim 6 or submit arguments pointing to a factual or structural difference that would overcome the asserted combination.",
      "support_doc_id": "I40JLR5YPXXIFW3",
