      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "Claims 3 and dependent/new claims 10–16 remain unpatentable under pre‑AIA 35 U.S.C. 103 over the cited combination. The examiner finds Walter teaches cleaning/rinsing and disposition of rinse solvent; Hayes teaches use of separate cleaning and rinse zones to reduce contamination of rinse liquid; Donnelly teaches distillation/recovery of contaminated solvent; Tonkovich teaches a micro‑still (distillation with bottoms removal and condenser). Combining these teachings would have been obvious to one of ordinary skill to implement continuous recovery and recycling of rinse solvent via a micro‑still, pump, level control, and condenser as recited in the pending claims.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "HTR7LS2ZPXXIFW4",
          "support_span": "Claims 3 and 10-16 are rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 103(a) as being unpatentable over Walter (U.S Patent 6,348,101 B1) in view of Hayes (U.S Patent 5,716,457) and Donnelly et al. (U.S Patent 6,159,345) and Tonkovich (PG Pub 20060016215).",
