rect that a single unrelated connector-contact example in Lee is not the same as predicting drillstring-to-wellbore contact points; however, the rejection does not rest on that connector example alone but on the combined teaching that modeling/simulation (Lee) informs predicted contact behavior and that Kennedy provides a reason to select locations for ranging devices. When considered together, the combination supports the asserted obviousness conclusion. If the applicant believes a narrower construction of \"drill string profile\" is required, prosecution may address claim language clarity under 35 U.S.C. 112 or propose amended claim language to more precisely recite the profile features.\nC. Applicant: Homan’s non-conductive tube covers transmitters/receivers and does not teach placing insulators between ranging devices as claimed.\nExaminer response: Homan teaches non-conductive tubes and fiber/resin constructions intended to allow electromagnetic instruments to be housed while providing non-conductive structure (the Office action cited Homan’s Abstract and related passages). Whether Homan’s drawings/text explicitly show every positional arrangement is a question of obviousness when combined with Lee and Kennedy: an artisan seeking to prevent unintended conductive contact between spaced ranging elements, having modeled predicted contact locations of a BHA (Lee) and having reason to select positions for ranging elements (Kennedy), would be expected to adapt Homan’s non-conductive sleeve teachings to insulate selected drillstring portions. The Office action articulated this combination and motivation (I3PX7NH5PXXIFW4: \"Therefore it would have been obvious ... to combine the insulator members/sleeves/tubes of Homan with the method of Lee as modified by Kennedy\"). The applicant’s argument that Homan primarily shows transmitters/receivers inside a tube does not negate that Homan teaches non-conductive sleeve/housing materials and structures that are directly applicable to insulating portions of a drillstring at selected locations. Thus the Examiner maintains the combination rejection.\n3) Allowable subject matter\nAs previously indicated in the December 15, 2014 Office action, claim 8 was identified as containing allowable subject matter because the recorded applied references did not sufficiently disclose or suggest evaluating harmonic frequencies of the drillstring under anticipated drilling conditions to determine additional insulator member requirements. That assessment remains. Claim 8 is currently treated as allowable for that reason unless new references or arguments are presented that would alter that determination.\nNext steps and options to applicant\n- If the applicant wishes to overcome the maintained 103 rejections, prosecution options include: (a) amendment of the claims to recite additional limitations distinguishing over the combined teachings of Lee, Kennedy and Homan or otherwise narrowing claim scope; (b) presenting persuasive evidence (e.g., a declaration under 37 C.F.R. 1.132) explaining why a skilled artisan would not have combined the cited teachings or why the cited references do not in fact disclose the claimed features; or (c) arguing claim construction differences or pointing to specific record evidence that distinguishes the claims from the combined prior art on points other than those addressed above.\n- If applicant files claim amendments, please annotate clearly the status of each claim (canceled, amended, new, or unchanged) and provide marked-up claim text. If relying on affidavits/declarations, identify the declarant’s qualifications and provide any supporting data.\n- If applicant wishes to request an expedited telephone interview to discuss the rejections and possible claim amendments, contact information is available in the file; the Examiner is willing to confer to clarify the cited prior art and discuss amendment strategy.\nConclusion\nThe Examiner has reviewed applicant’s February 24, 2015 remarks and amendments. The prior 35 U.S.C. 103 rejections of claims 1-7, 9, 12-16, and 18-20 over Lee in view of Kennedy and further in view of Homan are maintained for the reasons discussed above. Claim 8 remains allowable as previously indicated. Applicant is invited to respond by amendment and/or argument including any evidence to overcome the maintained rejections. If claims are amended, please provide marked and clean copies and point out specifically how the amendments distinguish over the cited combination of references.\nSaid action is non-final. No allowance is made at this time for the claims maintained as rejected. The Examiner is available for an interview if desired.",
