{
  "sample_id": "13981387_t1",
  "next_action_type": "CTNF",
  "claim_ground_evidence": [
    {
      "claim_ids": [1, 2, 4, 7, 8, 9, 11, 14],
      "ground": "102",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["HJIRVRJ9PXXIFW3"],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The cited reference Chao (US 5,145,658) was applied in the prior Office action (IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4) as disclosing the combination of an absorption column, a regeneration column, circulation/heat-exchange between lean and rich solutions, and steam produced from returning solution and supplied to the regenerator (see Fig. 2 and Example 2 of Chao). The previously-issued action set forth specific mappings between claim limitations and Chao (IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4). Applicant's A1 amendments and arguments do not persuasively establish that the cited Chao disclosure fails to disclose the claimed combination or that the existing rejection is erroneous. Therefore the anticipation rejection under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 102(b) for the identified claims is maintained at this time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4",
          "support_span": "Claims 1-2, 4, 7-9, 11, and 14 are rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 102(b) as being anticipated by US Patent No. 5,145,658 to Chao.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "pgpub_claims",
          "support_span": "\"1. A recovery apparatus of carbon dioxide comprising: an absorption column... a steam supply system configured to generate steam... and to supply the steam to the regeneration column.\"",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    },
    {
      "claim_ids": [3, 5, 6, 10, 12, 13],
      "ground": "103",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["HJIRVRJ9PXXIFW3"],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The prior action found these dependent claims would have been obvious in view of Chao in combination with conventional design choice(s) (e.g., adding a second steam generator, using multiple compressors in series). Applicant's A1 arguments do not provide persuasive factual or claim construction distinctions to overcome the asserted obviousness. The obviousness rejections under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 103(a) for these claims are therefore maintained.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4",
          "support_span": "Claims 3, 5-6, 10, and 12-13 are rejected under pre-AIA 35 U.S.C. 103(a) as being unpatentable over Chao.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    },
    {
      "claim_ids": [7, 14],
      "ground": "112b",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4","IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3"],
      "status": "withdrawn",
      "rationale": "The prior Office action rejected claims 7 and 14 as indefinite under 35 U.S.C. 112; applicant amended claim language in A1 to recite supplying 'a part of a quantity of heat ... to the absorbing liquid in the regeneration column by means of heat exchange with the absorbing liquid in the regeneration column,' which addresses the prior indefiniteness concern by clarifying the recipient and mechanism. The rejection under 112(b) is therefore withdrawn for these claims.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4",
          "support_span": "Claim 7 and 14 are rejected under 35 U.S.C. 112(b) ... as being indefinite",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3",
          "support_span": "The recovery apparatus of carbon dioxide according to claim 4, further comprising a heat exchanger for supplying a part of a quantity of heat of the steam that is raised in temperature by the compression device, to the absorbing liquid in the regeneration column by means of heat exchange with the absorbing liquid in the regeneration column.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    },
    {
      "claim_ids": [4],
      "ground": "objection",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4","IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3"],
      "status": "withdrawn",
      "rationale": "The earlier formal objection identified a missing word (\"temperature\") in claim 4. Applicant's A1 amendment corrected the phrasing in the claim. The formal objection is withdrawn.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4",
          "support_span": "Claim 4 is objected to because of the following informalities: In regard to claim 4, the term “temperature” is missing ... Appropriate correction is required.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        },
        {
          "doc_id": "IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3",
          "support_span": "a compression device configured to compress the generated steam to raise a temperature of the steam to be higher than a regeneration temperature of the absorbing liquid.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    },
    {
      "claim_ids": [15, 16],
      "ground": "other",
      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3"],
      "status": "new",
      "rationale": "Claims 15-16 are newly added in the A1 submission. They recite that the absorbing liquid includes an amine absorbent. Because these claims were not part of the previously-examined claim set, their patentability in view of the cited prior art has not yet been determined and remains outstanding/unresolved. Applicant is notified that the effective entry of amended/added claims is subject to formal entry of the amended claim set; the examiner will act on these claims after their formal entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "doc_id": "IE3AJE9GPXXIFW3",
          "support_span": "Claim 15 (New): The recovery apparatus of carbon dioxide according to claim 1,wherein the absorbing liquid includes an amine absorbant.",
          "source_scope": "record_text"
        }
      ],
      "evidence_status": "record_supported"
    }
  ],
  "applicant_argument_responses": [
    {
      "claim_ids": [1],
      "argument_summary": "Applicant argues Chao uses different scrubbing chemistry and that Chao's 'steam jet 186' is a vacuum-inducing device, not a compression device that raises steam temperature above the regenerator temperature; thus Chao does not teach compression-heated steam as claimed.",
      "response": "Applicant is correct that differences in working fluids (e.g., potassium carbonate vs. amine solutions) and differences in operating strategy can be relevant to patentability. However, the prior Office action relied on Chao's express disclosure of producing steam from solution and supplying steam to the regenerator, and on the Example 2 material and flow streams showing steam generation/processing. Where Chao discloses producing a lower-pressure vapor from solution and subsequently delivering hotter steam to the regenerator (see the Example 2 table and Fig. 2 mappings in IAFRWV4BPXXIFW4), the claimed functional result (steam generated from returning/absorbing liquid and provided to the regenerator as regeneration heat) is disclosed. The examiner notes Applicant's contention that Chao's 'steam jet 186' functions as an ejector/vacuum device rather than a mechanical compressor. The characterization of that device in Chao affects claim construction of Applicant's compression-device limitation. If Applicant contends that the claimed 'compression device' requires a mechanical compressor (and not an ejector or mixing device) or requires positive mechanical compression producing a temperature increase by compression work, Applicant should (1) propose claim language that clearly defines the required structure (for example, explicitly reciting a rotary or reciprocating compressor or a specified compression mechanism), or (2) submit evidence that Chao's steam jet cannot operate as a 'compression device' under the claim as properly construed. Without such amendment or persuasive evidence, the examiner continues to find that Chao reasonably suggests producing steam from solution and delivering heated steam to the regenerator, and that a person of ordinary skill could have made the claimed apparatus/steps based on Chao and common practice. Consequently, the 102/103 rejections are maintained for the previously applied claims. Applicant is invited to submit clarifying claim amendments, declarations, or technical evidence to support a narrower construction of 'compression device' if Applicant wishes to pursue patentable distinction.",
