      "claim_ids": [343, 344, 346, 349, 351, 353, 354, 355, 358, 359, 363, 365, 367, 372, 373, 374, 375],
      "argument_summary": "Applicant amended many claims (filed Sept. 19 and corrected Sept. 26, 2014) and argues that Eppstein, Jung and Aceti are topical/skin-applied devices whereas the amended claims require percutaneous/minimally invasive insertion/injection into tissue (i.e., implantable or injectable), delivery from an agent-containing matrix, self-activating release, and multiple reservoirs with comparative assay functionality; applicant requests allowance of the amended claims.",
      "response": "The applicant's amendments are acknowledged. However, the record supplied to the examiner for the March 19, 2014 Office action contained the earlier claim set (GKFY5I21PPOPPY2) and the rejections were made with respect to that examined claim set. The applicant's September 2014 amended claims were filed as a response and are therefore recorded as proposed claim changes (I0JYPE5NPXXIFW3). At this time the proposed amendments have not been entered (the entry status is unknown in the record). The examiner cannot treat the proposed claim set as replacing the claims that were examined in the March 19, 2014 Office action until the amendments are entered. If applicant wishes the examiner to consider the September 2014 amended claim set as the claim(s) of record, applicant must explicitly request entry of those amendments and, if necessary, provide clean replacement claim pages or a formal amendment that complies with 37 C.F.R. 1.121, and show the basis in the disclosure for any newly-added claim limitations.\nAccordingly: (1) For the claims that were examined in the March 19, 2014 Office action (those coming from GKFY5I21PPOPPY2 and listed as the examined/entered claim set in the record), the rejections and objections in that action are maintained for the reasons stated therein. (2) For the proposed amended claims filed September 19 and corrected September 26, 2014 (I0JYPE5NPXXIFW3), the examiner will consider entry upon applicant filing a request for entry and complying with formal entry requirements (clean replacement claims or a formal amendment identifying changes and showing support) and resolving any new formalities. Upon entry, the examiner will act on the merits of the entered amendments; applicant's substantive arguments about differences from the cited references will be considered at that time. At present the examiner cannot conclude that the cited references fail to anticipate or render obvious the claims of the March 19, 2014 examined set; and the examiner similarly cannot yet find allowance of the proposed claim set because it has not been entered. If applicant believes the amendments should be entered despite any outstanding formalities, state the basis and identify the specific supporting portions of the specification (page/paragraph or figure reference) for each newly-added limitation so the examiner can determine whether the amendment complies with the statutes and rules for entry.",
