      "claim_version_doc_ids": ["IPPLGGCBRXEAPX1","I2Y16E1VPXXIFW3","pgpub_description"],
      "status": "maintained",
      "rationale": "The prior art combination the examiner relied upon (Spruce et al. and Kusiak et al., with Hammerum for trailing-edge flaps) continues to teach the principal features of the independent and dependent claims as construed for examination: predictive wind sensing (LIDAR), a predictive controller optimizing an energy-related cost function over a finite horizon, and control of generator torque and blade pitch. Applicant amended claim 1 to recite particular cost functions (converted aerodynamic energy; electrical energy plus kinetic energy; or electrical energy while setting a boundary condition on rotor speed). The cited art, when viewed as a whole and under the Examiner's reasonable claim construction used for prosecution, still discloses or makes obvious these alternatives: Kusiak addresses maximizing energy capture and includes energy/rotor-speed dynamics; Spruce discloses LIDAR-based prediction and predictive controller optimizing a cost function; Hammerum discloses deformable trailing-edge sections. The combination and motivation (improving energy capture using predictive wind information and predictive control) render the claimed subject matter obvious as previously set forth.",
