      "argument_summary": "Applicant argues that 'a rotor swept area of the wind turbine' is defined in the specification (area swept by the blades) and thus is not indefinite.",
      "response": "The Examiner acknowledges the specification passages that describe the rotor swept area (see pgpub_description; e.g., 'rotor swept area (the area swept by the blades of the wind turbine)'). However, the remaining claim language still leaves ambiguity as to whether the claim recites an additional method step ('assuming the wind speed value') or merely a limitation on previously recited estimating steps. To cure the outstanding indefiniteness the Examiner recommends (and invites) either: (1) amend the claim to make clear whether this is (i) an additional method step (e.g., 'further comprising assuming that the representative future wind speed values are constant across the rotor swept area') or (ii) a limitation (e.g., 'wherein the representative future wind speed values are assumed to be constant across the rotor swept area'), and (2) use plural form consistently if multiple values are intended (e.g., 'values' rather than 'value').",
