      "response": "For prosecution, the Examiner construes the recitation to require that the control strategy utilize either a linear or non-linear predictive model (this narrower construction is used to enable meaningful prior-art comparison). If Applicant intends broader functional language, Applicant should supply claim language tied to specific model features or algorithmic steps disclosed in the specification (e.g., optimization horizon length, prediction model equations, explicit constraints, optimizer type). Alternatively, Applicant may identify specific passages in the specification that clearly and unambiguously support the current claim language to overcome the 112(b) objections. Absent such amendment or clear support, the Examiner will continue to treat the claim language under the stated construction for prior-art comparison.",
